/target
*.pb.bin
testing/diffrig/captures/

# Markdown is ignored by default so scratch notes don't accumulate in history.
# Everything below is re-included because it is LOAD-BEARING: each is cited by
# name from tracked source, so a fresh clone without it has dead links.
#
# The planning docs were local-only until 2026-08-01. That stopped being
# tenable once the code started citing them — `git grep` counts ADR-0004 55
# times, ADR-0003 34, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md 30, docs/envoy-divergences.md 13.
# A `// see ADR-0004` comment pointing at a file nobody else has is worse than
# no comment. They also had no backup: WP-45's design existed in exactly one
# place, on one laptop, which is the same failure mode as CLAUDE.md rule 10
# with a different cause.
*.md
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!.claude/**/*.md
!testing/corpus/fixtures/**/SOURCES.md
# The spec the Go QA suite is written from — reviewable alongside the tests
# that cite its case IDs.
!testing/qa/SCENARIOS.md
# Normative plan, milestone/ship-gate definitions, and architecture decisions.
!PLAN.md
!IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
!docs/**/*.md
